    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d324">

                <pb facs="0493" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Hillfern/130: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Antwerp</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Antwerp</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-05-21T11:00:00+01:00">May 21, 1936—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 21—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My May 19, 10 p.m.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d324-f1"/> Following our representations
                    to Maritime Commissioner of the Port <hi rendition="#italic">Hillfern</hi>
                    seized and formal inquiry ordered. Telegraphic instructions from Minister of
                    Marine ordered release of ship and abandonment of inquiry. She is now at liberty
                    to sail at any time. She is, however, berthed near customs to permit constant
                    surveillance.</p>
                <p>Meeus has informed customs that he believed he had found purchaser in Rotterdam
                    for alcohol, that ship would probably clear therefor shortly and that ultimate
                    destination of alcohol would be Switzerland. Prospective purchaser expected
                    Antwerp Friday to inspect alcohol and close deal.</p>
                <p>Consul Rotterdam informed.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
